<title>RUSSIA: Moscow to examine black boxes from India crash.</title>
<headline>Moscow to examine black boxes from India crash.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian experts will decode information from &quot;black box&quot; flight recorders recovered from the Kazakh cargo plane which crashed in mid-air with a Saudi jumbo jet near New Delhi, an official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The black boxes would soon be brought to Moscow from India, said the official at the Interstate Aviation Committee which handles air transport matters for the 12 former Soviet republics grouped in the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS).</p>
<p>The Ilyushin Il-76 cargo plane was chartered by a Kyrgyz company from the state-owned Kazakhstan National Airways.</p>
<p>Some 350 people aboard the two planes are feared to have died in the crash over India.</p>
